From f829d7ee1ab415369ca7f91da51aaa1c81fd60df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:33:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build: Docker builds for the shipped Linux target (and
 documented cross/native rules)

docker/linux.Dockerfile rebuilds the release linux job's tar.gz, deb, rpm
and AppImage in a container: ubuntu:22.04 pinned by digest, the job's apt
list verbatim, the same cargo build line, package-linux.sh and
package-appimage.sh with the same pinned linuxdeploy SHA-256, and the
job's package-content checks. docker/windows-gnu.Dockerfile cross-builds
an unofficial x86_64-pc-windows-gnu portable zip with mingw-w64.
docker/README.md states per shipped target whether it builds in Docker and
why snap, Flatpak, the msvc Windows zip + installer and macOS stay on
their runners. No workflow added (local tooling, no Actions minutes).

Fixes #30

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
